# Vocabulary

One word for one thing, everywhere: buttons, headings, errors, notifications, docs. Voice: {{VOICE}}.

{{DEFAULTS_NOTE}}

## Voice

Sentence case. Plain words. Say what happened and what to do next. No exclamation marks, no blame, no jargon the audience
({{AUDIENCE}}) would not use.

## Product words

| We say | We never say | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| _to fill_ | _to fill_ | The product's own nouns, filled from the interview or extracted from the screens. |

## Actions (button verbs)

Verb plus object: "Save changes", "Add member", "Delete project". Primary action first. Cancel is "Cancel", never "No".
Destructive confirmations repeat the verb: "Delete project", not "OK".

| Do | Not |
|---|---|
| Save, Add, Delete, Remove | Submit, Go, OK, Yes |
| Sign in, Sign out | Log in, Login, Logout |
| Cancel | Dismiss, Abort |

## Status words

Status is a word plus an icon. Pick one word per state and keep it: e.g. Draft, Active, Done, Failed. Add the product's own
set here.

## Dates, times, numbers, durations

Pick one format per kind and use one formatter for it (web: one helper module; mobile: one formatter). Numbers in tables
are tabular and right-aligned. Plurals read correctly for zero and one.

## Errors, empty states, confirmations

Error: what happened, what to do. Empty: what is missing, why, one action. Confirmation: what changed, in the past tense.
